    },
    {
      "id": 496304,
      "username": "KEVINAMAYI",
      "name": "Kevin Amayi Musungu",
      "created_at": "2026-03-24T07:57:00.983Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Thanks for the suggestion, but this is happening during a Data Import job — not from manually editing a form. The timestamp conflict occurs entirely within the import process itself, with no human interaction involved.</p>\n<p>You can see this in the timestamps:<br>\n• 22:07:14 — importer opens the document<br>\n• 22:14:01 — importer tries to save it</p>\n<p>That’s a 7-minute gap caused by the importer’s own internal writes racing against each other. Refreshing the page doesn’t apply here.</p>\n<p>This is also happening across multiple sites immediately after upgrading to v15.101.3, which points to a regression in the Data Import background job logic rather than a UI/session issue.</p>",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discuss.frappe.io/kevinamayi/{size}/88853_2.png",
      "trust_level": 1,
      "post_number": 3,
      "post_type": 1,
      "like_count": null,
      "like_action": null,
      "Reads": 10,
      "wikis": null,
      "can_edit": false,
      "can_delete": false,
      "can_recover": false,
      "can_view_edit_history": true,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "version": 1,
      "last_edited_at": null,
      "edited_at": null
    },
    {
      "id": 496321,
      "username": "tcbinfotech",
      "name": "TCB Infotech",
      "created_at": "2026-03-24T10:08:14.071Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Got it, thanks for the clarification. Since this is happening within the Data Import job itself and across multiple sites post v15.101.3 upgrade, it does look like a regression in the background import process rather than a user/session issue. The 7-minute gap clearly indicates internal write conflicts. This likely needs a fix at the framework level.</p>",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discuss.frappe.io/tcbinfotech/{size}/93928_2.png",
      "trust_level": 2,
      "post_number": 4,
      "post_type": 1,
      "like_count": null,
      "like_action": null,
      "Reads": 10,
